(4088416, 577522, 63267, '<td valign="top">Just got home from vacation and this is the first photo I have seen on here.  This is such an awesome shot, and a top 5 finish and a new personal best as well.  I am so happy for you!  Congratulations!!!</td>', 'Just got home from vacation and this is the first photo I have seen on here.  This is such an awesome shot, and a top 5 finish and a new personal best as well.  I am so happy for you!  Congratulations!!!', '2007-09-13 22:33:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4088991, 578132, 65592, '<td valign="top">I have to dissagree with you. If you wish to show motion and speed in your picture it would be better a panning shot rather than cropping the horse''s tail. Maybe in another kind of picture the crop will work, but this is not the case IMO. When I look at this picture I do not feel motion, the only I see is a sharp picture of a frozen horse floating on the air. Just my opinion, maybe in a more professional forum you will get a different opinion...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-09-14 09:43:49.</i></td>', 'I have to dissagree with you. If you wish to show motion and speed in your picture it would be better a panning shot rather than cropping the horse''s tail. Maybe in another kind of picture the crop will work, but this is not the case IMO. When I look at this picture I do not feel motion, the only I see is a sharp picture of a frozen horse floating on the air. Just my opinion, maybe in a more professional forum you will get a different opinion...', '2007-09-14 05:50:14.000000', '2007-09-14 10:43:49.000000', 0),
(4089732, 577522, 35322, '<td valign="top">Wow! This is stunning. There is so much life in this pic, it''s vibrant! I wanna be there and play with them! And I like the b&amp;w conversion.</td>', 'Wow! This is stunning. There is so much life in this pic, it''s vibrant! I wanna be there and play with them! And I like the b&w conversion.', '2007-09-14 12:20:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4092565, 578647, 1031, '<td valign="top">Big bold color patches give it a great painterly look (Van Gogh, Gaugin?) -- this might have fared better in the Impressionism challenge, where I suspect people were more tolerant of blur.<br/> <br/>Personally, I think I''d mask off and darken the background showing on the left side, especially the sky area, as it really tends to pull the eye towards the upper-left corner, in the opposite direction of your subject''s motion. I think making it darker would reduce the effect.<br/> <br/>Now I have to check and see if I don''t have some blurry pictures of <b>my</b> kid on a slide ... ;-)<br/> <br/>Nice work.</td>', 'Big bold color patches give it a great painterly look (Van Gogh, Gaugin?) -- this might have fared better in the Impressionism challenge, where I suspect people were more tolerant of blur. Personally, I think I''d mask off and darken the background showing on the left side, especially the sky area, as it really tends to pull the eye towards the upper-left corner, in the opposite direction of your subject''s motion. I think making it darker would reduce the effect. Now I have to check and see if I don''t have some blurry pictures of my kid on a slide ... ;-) Nice work.', '2007-09-15 22:51:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4092672, 578647, 69008, '<td valign="top">It fits this "Blur" side challenge very well. There is big fun going on in this image. I can almost hear the squeals of pleasure.</td>', 'It fits this "Blur" side challenge very well. There is big fun going on in this image. I can almost hear the squeals of pleasure.', '2007-09-15 23:49:13.000000', NULL, 0),
